---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
import SpecList from '../components/SpecList.astro';
import Pending from '../components/Pending.astro';
import Action from '../components/Action.astro';
import { COMPANY, ADDRESS_LINE, EMAIL_HREF, UNKNOWNS } from '../data/company.ts';
import { PAGES } from '../data/site.ts';

const meta = PAGES[1]!;
---
<Base title={meta.title} description={meta.description}>
  <Field tone="forest" reveal={false}>
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>The mill is running again.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A redwood mill has stood on Kunzler Ranch Road for more than forty years.
        In 2025 it went back into local family hands.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="paper">
    <!-- Prose may name the road; only the record and the footer carry the full
         canonical citation "650 Kunzler Ranch Rd, Ukiah, CA 95482". A road name
         with no street number, city or postcode is not a competing NAP citation,
         and the history reads badly with an abbreviation in the middle of it. -->
    <h2>Where this comes from.</h2>
    <p class="prose gap">
      The Agwood name has been on a redwood mill in Ukiah since the early 1980s. In
      2017 the business and its assets were sold to Conrad Forest Products of North
      Bend, Oregon. In 2025 the mill came back under local family
      ownership, keeping the name and the site on Kunzler Ranch Road.
    </p>
    <!--
      This paragraph is doing real work and should not be cut as throat-clearing.

      The public record for this company is genuinely contradictory: live listings
      disagree on the street address, the telephone, the legal entity and the number
      of locations, because several of them describe the pre-2017 business. A buyer
      who searches the company before calling WILL find those. Explaining the break
      turns the most confusing thing about Agwood's search results into evidence
      that this site is the accurate one — which is the second job this site exists
      to do. See PRODUCT.md, "Operating Context".
    -->
    <p class="prose">
      That break is worth stating plainly, because a search will turn up listings
      from both eras. The address, telephone and hours on this site are the current
      ones.
    </p>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="deep">
    <h2>One species, run properly.</h2>
    <p class="prose gap">
      Redwood is the only timber we mill. That is a choice about attention rather
      than a limit on capacity: grading redwood consistently means knowing how this
      wood moves, splits and seasons, and that knowledge does not transfer from one
      species to the next.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      We sell to lumber retailers and distributors across Northern California. They
      resell what we grade, under their own name, to customers we never meet. That
      only works if what is on the sticker is what is in the pack.
    </p>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="paper">
    <h2 class="ttl label">Regulation</h2>
    <!--
      Deliberately narrow, and it must stay that way.

      The client approved stating the Forest Practice Act as jurisdictional context.
      Its permitted scope is exactly that: a fact about California law. It may NOT be
      rewritten to describe Agwood's own sourcing or to imply a certification the
      company does not hold — we do not know where their logs come from. The second
      sentence is the safety valve and must not be deleted to tidy the paragraph.
    -->
    <p class="prose">
      Timber harvested on private and industrial land in California is governed by
      the California Forest Practice Act, which requires approved harvest plans
      covering water quality, erosion and replanting. Agwood holds no FSC or SFI
      certification and does not claim one.
    </p>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="deep">
    <h2 class="ttl label">The record</h2>
    <SpecList rows={[
      { term: 'Company', value: COMPANY.name },
      { term: 'Ownership', value: 'Family-owned' },
      { term: 'Location', value: ADDRESS_LINE },
      { term: 'County', value: 'Mendocino County, California' },
      { term: 'Species', value: 'Redwood only' },
      { term: 'Products', value: COMPANY.products.join(' · ') },
      { term: 'Sells to', value: 'Retailers and distributors' },
      { term: 'Hours', value: COMPANY.hours.display },
      { term: UNKNOWNS[0]!.field, value: UNKNOWNS[0]!.say, unknown: true },
    ]} />
  </Field>

  <Field tone="paper">
    <h2 class="ttl label">Still to come</h2>
    <Pending
      label="Photographs of the mill, the yard and the crew"
      note="Agwood owns no photographs of its own operation yet. Nothing on this site is a stock photograph standing in for one."
    />
  </Field>

  <Field tone="deep">
    <h2>Talk to the mill.</h2>
    <p class="prose gap">Email is the quickest way to reach us with an enquiry.</p>
    <p class="cta"><Action href={EMAIL_HREF}>Email the mill</Action></p>
  </Field>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero h1 { max-width: 13ch; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.4rem); }
  .hero .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 42ch; }
  .ttl { color: var(--russet); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-body); }
  .gap { margin-bottom: var(--stack); }
  .cta { margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
